# ---- Pool bake fan-out cap (hub only, optional — 2 is the default) ----
# The debounce decides WHETHER a pool bakes this tick; this decides HOW MANY at
# once. On 2026-09-20 00:00Z the first tick after midnight met a freshly rolled
# WARM_BUST — every warm layer cold on the same tick — and ten full builds went
# at one Fly remote builder: one OOM'd, five starved past the timeout.
#   POOL_BAKE_PARALLEL      the most bakes of pools whose warm layer is CURRENT
#                           that bin/fleet-propagate.sh runs at once. Default 2.
#                           0 = unlimited, the behaviour before this knob.
#                           An unparseable value logs one line and uses 2.
# A pool whose last ok bake is not from TODAY is cold (its bake pays for the
# whole checkout + install + build) and is ALWAYS baked one at a time, in a
# serial lane beside the capped one — so the ceiling is POOL_BAKE_PARALLEL + 1
# remote builds, whatever this is set to. `fleet-propagate.sh --check` prints
# the lane it would use per pool. See docs/verification-map/pool-bake-fanout.md.
#POOL_BAKE_PARALLEL=2

